e glycerol stock option that i  mentioned  those are always provided as one guide  per well it's only the lentiviral  particles that we ever do  um as a pool  awesome you think you got one or two  more in yeah i know we've had you  talking for  for about an hour now let's let's find  one more  yeah great all right about um  about selection and and delivering  one or both vectors oh yeah i think  that's this one here  okay so let me read this okay yeah so if  you deliver cas9 via one vector and the  guide rna on another vector  is it possible for only one of the  vectors to get into the cell  yeah so of course it's possible um  you know so generally speaking um  it is that's why it's recommended for  screening especially that you would  produce a cas9 stable cell line  certainly the only delivery variable you  have  is um with with that guide rna  but if you do a co-transduction with the  cas9 and the guide  as i said of course it's possible only  one gets in so then you could just do  you know selection with both um of  antibiotic resistance  uh markers um but you may not even need  to do selection at all you might just be  able to directly assay for knockout  um with the assumption that enough of  your cell population  got both the cas9 and the guide and  you're able to see it so some of that's  just going to depend on  the overall efficiency  our final comments here and i just  wanted to say before we go i i want to  thank um  thank you luis for uh for your great  presentation  and thank our audience for joining us  today um as i said in the opening  questions that we did not get time to  answer  or any of those that come in from during  the on-demand period  will be addressed by email that you  provided during your registration  uh we'd like to thank lab roots for  hosting this for us  and thermo fisher scientific for  underwriting today's educational webcast  this can be viewed on demand in the  future lab roots will alert you by email  when this is available fo